# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored (`.gitignore`'s `.env*` rule)
# and must never be committed. No real value belongs in THIS file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The RESTRICTED APPLICATION ROLE, used for all request-serving traffic.
#
# Point this at `app_runtime` (or an equivalently scoped role) — NOT at the
# Supabase `postgres` superuser-adjacent role. `app_runtime` is provisioned with
# LOGIN, NOSUPERUSER, NOBYPASSRLS, NOCREATEDB, NOCREATEROLE, NOREPLICATION, and
# holds exactly USAGE on schema `public` plus SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on its
# tables (no TRUNCATE, REFERENCES or TRIGGER). It does not own the tables.
#
# That combination is what makes the `tenant_isolation` RLS policies a real
# security boundary: Postgres exempts a BYPASSRLS role from RLS unconditionally,
# and FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY cannot override it. Pointing this variable at
# `postgres` silently disables every RLS policy in the schema for application
# traffic while leaving the policies themselves looking perfectly correct.
#
# Use the POOLED, transaction-mode Supabase endpoint (port 6543, with
# `?pgbouncer=true`). Note that Supabase's pooler encodes tenant routing in the
# username, so the user component is `app_runtime.<project-ref>`, not bare
# `app_runtime`.
#
# Format: postgresql://app_runtime.<project-ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true
DATABASE_URL=

# The OWNER role, used only for `prisma migrate dev` / `prisma migrate deploy`
# (see prisma.config.ts) and for `prisma db seed`. DDL, CREATE POLICY and
# ALTER TABLE all need owner-level privileges that `app_runtime` is deliberately
# denied. Unpooled, session-mode endpoint (port 5432). This stays on `postgres`
# in every environment, test runs included.
#
# Format: postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>:5432/postgres
DIRECT_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env.test` — local test runs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is also a gitignored `.env.test`, loaded ON TOP OF `.env` when
# NODE_ENV=test (Vitest sets this automatically). See src/db/env.ts.
#
# Its only job is to override DATABASE_URL back to the owner role for test runs.
# Tasks 3-8's schema-verification tests and prisma/seed.ts are a sanctioned
# pattern that imports `rawPrisma` directly and issues reads and writes with no
# tenant context, because they exercise schema and constraints from outside the
# request-handling layer — statements that RLS correctly refuses to
# `app_runtime`. tests/db/runtime-role-rls.test.ts deliberately reads `.env`
# itself, so the restricted role is still proved end-to-end.
#
# To create it, copy your pre-hardening (owner) DATABASE_URL into:
#   DATABASE_URL=<the DIRECT/owner credentials on the pooled 6543 endpoint>
# DIRECT_URL needs no override.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth (Auth.js / NextAuth v5 — Credentials provider, Prisma adapter, DB sessions)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Billing (Stripe, first provider behind the §6 interface boundary)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage (Supabase Storage, first provider behind the §7 interface boundary)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage is a separate Supabase service: its tables live in the `storage`
# schema with their own grants, and its server-side path authenticates with the
# service-role key below. It is unaffected by the hardening that revoked
# `anon`/`authenticated` privileges on the `public` schema.
#
# The service-role key bypasses RLS by design — it is a server-only secret and
# must never be exposed to the browser.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email (Resend for transactional emails)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=noreply@equestrianloop.com
